    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48108" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεμελῐ-όω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to lay the foundation of, found firmly</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πύργους . . φοίνιξι θεμελιώσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					7.5.11
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(2).11.26
			</span></i> (Mytil.), <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Jo.</u>
				6.25
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				26
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ep.Hebr.</u>
				1.10
			</span></i>, etc.:—
				Pass.
			, <i>have the foundations laid,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				22.1343.15
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i B.C.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ τὴν πέτραν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
					7.25
				</span></i>
			: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βασιλεία καλῶς θεμελιωθεῖσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					11.68
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡγεμονία κάλλιστα τεθεμελιωμένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					15.1
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ἀγάπῃ τεθ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ep.Eph.</u>
				3.18
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ πίστει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ep.Col.</u>
					1.23
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>destroy utterly</i>, in 
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ωθέντα </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεμειλωθ-</span> cod.)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">:
				ἐκ ῥιζῶν ἀρθέντα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
